## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix Effort | Rationale |
|----------|-------|-----------|-----------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | Low | Prevents false-pass — highest risk |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | Low | Split into two simple tests |
| 3 | Mystery Guest | Low | Inline CSV data, removes env dependency |
| 4 | Sleepy Test | Medium | Requires async refactor or sync API |
| 5 | Exception Handling | Low | One-line swap to `Assert.ThrowsException` |
| 6 | Magic Number Test | Low | Add named constants |
| 7 | Sensitive Equality | Medium | Need to expose properties on summary type |
| 8 | Eager Test | Medium | Extract individual unit tests |
| 9 | General Fixture | Low | Delete unused field |

Start with priorities 1–3 — they eliminate false-confidence and environment-coupling risks with minimal effort.
